note Exercism-style exercise "acronym": https://exercism.org/tracks/python/exercises/acronym
note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note abbreviate writes the upper-case acronym of phrase s into o and returns its length. Words are
note separated by spaces, hyphens and other punctuation; an apostrophe does not start a new word.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/acronym
om2
fn abbreviate s view uchar * o edit uchar * to ulong
note replace this line with your solution
trap 13
end
